@blutmai_normal

= May Day, 1929

Tensions run high in Berlin. The annual Labor Day celebrations are on the first of May, but this coincides with the 10th Anniversary of the Comintern's Founding. The Communists are planning a demonstration to commemorate the occassion, but many are suspicious of their motives. 

Many non-communists are afraid of the possibility of another violent uprising, and our allies in the Prussian coalition are asking the Prussian Interior Ministry to ban the demonstrations.

Our party would like to celebrate Labor Day, but that would risk upsetting both sides. The Bourgeois parties would look upon it with suspicion, and the [+ uspd_name +] has not forgotten that it was our party members who ordered the Spartacist uprising's suppression, and the Communists still blame us for the deaths of Rosa Luxemburg and Karl Liebknecht.

- @ban: Ban the demonstrations.
- @allow_police: Allow the demonstrations to proceed, but maintain a heavy police presence.
- @allow: Allow the demonstrations to proceed unhindered, but keep our own celebrations separate.
- @join_conditional: Join in the demonstrations ourselves, but on the condition the demonstrations are explicitly for Labor Day, not the Comintern's Anniversary.
- @join: Join in the demonstrations ourselves.

@ban
on-arrival: blutmai = 1; uspd_relation -= 25; z_relation += 5; dvp_relation += 5; workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 3; workers_uspd += 3; unemployed_uspd += 3; communist_coalition -= 3; strife += 1
face-image: img/blutmai.jpg

We issued the order to ban the demonstrations, and sent police to enforce the ban. There was a confrontation between the police and Communists, and violence erupted. Reports say that the Berlin police killed dozens of demonstrators and innocent bystanders. The Communists are already calling this incident *Blutmai*, "Bloody May".

This may end any attempt at reconciliation with the [+ uspd_name +], but the Center and People's parties approve of our action.

- @corrupt_police: It is the fault of corrupt and reactionary elements within the police. Purge those responsible.
- @communist_fault: It is the fault of the Communists for refusing to follow the rule of law.
- @no_fault: It is an unfortunate incident that should not have happened, but is no one's fault at all.

@corrupt_police
on-arrival: uspd_relation += 10; z_relation -= 2; dvp_relation -= 2; prussian_police_loyalty += 0.05

We arrested the police responsible for the killings, and put them on trial. [? if judicial_reform = 0 : Unfortunately, the reactionary judiciary let them go free with barely any punishment at all. ?]

This assuages some of the Communists' outrage, but certainly not all.

@communist_fault
on-arrival: uspd_relation -= 10; z_relation += 5; dvp_relation += 5; rfb_strength -= 80; rfb_banned = 1

If the [+ uspd_name +] continues to act illegally, they must suffer the consequences. Thus, we have banned the RFKB, their paramilitary group. The bourgeois and right-leaning parties approve.

@no_fault

This position gains us no allies, and does not alienate anyone any further.


@allow_police
on-arrival: uspd_relation += 5; workers_uspd += 5; unemployed_uspd += 5

The demonstration proceeds peacefully under the watchful eyes of the police. Onlookers admire the strength of the Communist workers, and perhaps some of our supporters have been peeled off.

@allow
on-arrival: workers_uspd += 5; unemployed_uspd += 5; uspd_relation += 10; rfb_strength += 50; z_relation -= 3; dvp_relation -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1; rfb_militancy += 0.1

The demonstration proceeds peacefully, with a minimal police presence, while ours take place separately. Onlookers admire the strength of the Communist workers while our celebrations are somewhat overshadowed, and perhaps some of our members have been peeled off. The [+ uspd_name +] will never admit it, but they are developing a less hostile view towards us (even if they do not *like* us yet). Our centrist allies denounce the demonstration, but their cries are ineffectual.

@join_conditional
choose-if: uspd_relation >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: The Communists do not trust us enough.
on-arrival: uspd_relation += 10; workers_uspd += 4; unemployed_uspd += 4; workers_spd += 4; unemployed_spd += 4; new_middle_spd -= 3; old_middle_spd -= 3; z_relation -= 8; dvp_relation -= 8; coalition_dissent += 2; communist_coalition += 1; rfb_strength += 50; rfb_militancy += 0.1; sa_strength += 50; sh_strength += 50
achievement: die_rote_fahne

It is difficult to persuade the Communists to let us march with them, given the histories of their party and ours, especially considering the conditional nature of our offer. However, they eventually relent. The display of proletarian unity inspires the workers and worries the bourgeoisie and middle class, although some in our party tout this as proof we are taming the [+ uspd_name +]. [? if in_grand_coalition : Our coalition partners in the government are outraged at our display with the communists, and are threatening to break up the government. ?] The far-right paramilitaries increase their recruitment to counter us.

@join
choose-if: uspd_relation >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: The Communists do not trust us enough.
on-arrival: uspd_relation += 15; workers_uspd += 5; unemployed_uspd += 5; workers_spd += 5; unemployed_spd += 5; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 5; z_relation -= 10; dvp_relation -= 10; coalition_dissent += 2; communist_coalition += 2; rfb_strength += 100; rfb_militancy += 0.1; sa_strength += 50; sh_strength += 50
achievement: die_rote_fahne

It is difficult to persuade the Communists to let us march with them, given the histories of their party and ours. However, they eventually relent. The display of proletarian unity inspires the workers and terrifies the bourgeoisie and middle class. [? if in_grand_coalition : Our coalition partners in the government are outraged at our display with the communists, and are threatening to break up the government. ?] The far-right paramilitaries increase their recruitment to counter us.

@blutmai_right

= May Day, 1929

Tensions run high in Berlin. The Communists are planning a demonstration to commemorate the 10th anniversary of the Spartacist Uprising, in defiance of a ban on public gatherings in Berlin made by the right-wing government, which fears the possibility of another violent uprising.

Many on our party's left-wing have called on us to join in the demonstration, but this would only increase the risk of violence and could make reconciliation with the right-wing parties impossible. What should we do?

- @join_them: We will join in the demonstration.
- @not: We will stay out of this.

@join_them
choose-if: kpd_relation >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: The KPD does not trust us enough.
on-arrival: kpd_relation += 20; volksmai = 1; z_relation -= 10; z_relation -= 5 if z_party_leader != "Joos"; dvp_relation -= 25; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd -= 5; new_middle_spd += 3 if new_middle_conscious; old_middle_spd -= 5; unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent); workers_kpd += 3; unemployed_kpd += 3; workers_z -= 3; workers_dnvp -= 3; communist_coalition += 2; reformist_strength -= 10; reformist_dissent += 10; neorevisionist_dissent += 10; left_strength += 10; rfb_banned = 1; rfb_strength -= 100; strife += 2; socialism += 4
achievement: die_rote_fahne
face-image: img/blutmai.jpg

We join in the demonstrations, though most of the party right boycott and refuse to participate. The police are sent to disperse our demonstration and violence erupts. Reports say that the Berlin police killed dozens of demonstrators and innocent bystanders. We are already calling this incident *Blutmai*, "Bloody May".

This may end any attempt at reconciliation with the right, but the Communists approve of our action.


@not
on-arrival: kpd_relation -= 5; left_dissent += 5; workers_kpd += 3; unemployed_kpd += 3; rfb_banned = 1; rfb_strength -= 100; strife += 1; socialism -= 2

We do not participate in the demonstration, and it is a good thing that we didn't as it erupts into violence when the police are sent to disperse the Communists. Reports say that the Berlin police killed dozens of demonstrators and innocent bystanders. The Communists are already calling this incident *Blutmai*, "Bloody May".

What is our party's position?

- @dont: The party will not adopt a position on this tragedy.
- @pacifism: We condemn political violence on all sides, and this is another case of that.
- @pro_kpd: It is the fault of corrupt and reactionary elements within the police, which we will purge, and the government that directed them. 
- @pro_z: It is the fault of the Communists for refusing to follow the rule of law.

@dont

It is not our place to campaign on a tragedy that did not involve us.

@pacifism
on-arrival: workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); pacifism += 1; dvp_relation -= 5; kpd_relation -= 5; left_dissent += 5; rb_militancy -= 0.05; sh_militancy -= 0.02; rfb_militancy -= 0.02

What happened is a tragedy of political violence, and we will use this as an opportunity to direct our campaigning towards pacifistic messaging and urge against violence on all sides of the political spectrum, regardless of affiliation. 

@pro_kpd
on-arrival: workers_z -= 3; workers_dnvp -= 3; workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd -= 2; new_middle_spd -= 1 if not new_middle_conscious; kpd_relation += 10; z_relation -= 5; dvp_relation -= 10; prussian_police_loyalty += 0.05; reformist_dissent += 5; socialism += 1

What happened is the fault of the police who suppressed the demonstration, and the right-wing government's fault for ordering it. We will use our power in the Prussian Interior Ministry to purge those responsible, while blaming the government for the incident in official party communications.

@pro_z
on-arrival: new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd -= 1; kpd_relation -= 10; z_relation += 10; dvp_relation += 5; left_dissent += 15

What happened is the fault of the Communists for defying the rule of law and holding the demonstration in spite of the ban. We will defend the actions of the government, and the Prussian police force which we control, in the incident.
